Package: brilliant-flashing-tool
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Brilliant Flashing Tool <legendary-brilliantforous@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Legendary-Brilliantforous/brilliant-flashing-tool
Depends: @PYTHON_DEP@
Recommends: adb, lz4
Description: Open-source FRP reset and firmware flashing toolbox
 A Linux-native equivalent of the paid Windows flashing suites: one tool that
 talks directly to the bootloader of Samsung, MediaTek, Qualcomm and
 Spreadtrum/UNISOC phones.
 .
  * 8 transport modes (ADB, MTP, Download mode, Samsung BROM, MTK, MTK BROM,
    Fastboot, Qualcomm EDL) and ~120 operation methods.
  * Reverse-engineered Odin session protocol (Heimdall-based), PIT read/write,
    MediaTek BROM/DA flashing (scatter + GPT), Qualcomm Sahara/Firehose,
    UNISOC BSL, plus ADB/MTP/AT plumbing.
  * FRP bypass, screen-lock removal, MDM unlock, partition backup, network and
    battery repair, carrier-lock status checks.
  * Native Rust core (brilliant-bridge) with vendored libusb - no system USB
    dependencies beyond the shipped udev rules.
  * Bundled Python venv (PyQt6 + segno) - only the matching python3 minor is
    required, no distro Qt packages.
 .
 NOTE: the proprietary Samsung odin4 binary is not redistributed; fetch it
 after install with /usr/share/brilliant/scripts/fetch-odin4.sh.
 .
 WARNING: this tool talks directly to bootloaders and can wipe data or brick a
 device. Use only on devices you own or are authorized to service.
